      'Printing an array directly gives something useless like `[I@1b6d3586` \u2014 the type and hash. `Arrays.toString(arr)` produces the readable `[1, 2, 3]` form.\n\nThe rest of `java.util.Arrays`:\n- `Arrays.sort(arr)` sorts in place\n- `Arrays.fill(arr, value)` sets every element\n- `Arrays.copyOf(arr, newLength)` copies, padding or truncating\n- `Arrays.equals(a, b)` compares contents, since `==` compares references\n- `Arrays.binarySearch(arr, value)` searches a **sorted** array\n- `Arrays.stream(arr).sum()` for aggregates\n\nRemember to `import java.util.Arrays;`.',
